{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124372","id":4817586071,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHyaHlw","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124372","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124372.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124372.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124372/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124372/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124372/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/75c36547d460b564b3a0f9567528a12c080c9d42","number":124372,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Debugger: Add dual-channel protocol v2 for Godot 3.6","user":{"login":"nowasm","id":129167415,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7LwNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129167415?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm","html_url":"https://github.com/nowasm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nowasm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n- Introduce a versioned, dual-channel debugger protocol for Godot 3.6, separating execution control from bounded output and inspection traffic.\n- Add acknowledged control commands, heartbeat/disconnect recovery, lazy paged variable inspection, and a matching built-in editor frontend.\n- Add black-box tests for pairing, stepping, reconnects, backpressure, variable paging, and editor behavior.\n\n## Motivation\nThe existing single-stream debugger became unreliable under high output and large paused-state payloads in a large GDScript project. The new control channel keeps step/continue responsive when data traffic is saturated.\n\n## Verification\n- Built from the current `3.6` branch on Windows with `scons platform=windows tools=yes target=release_debug -j8`.\n- Protocol/session model checks and all 9 black-box runtime scenarios passed against the newly built binary.\n- Built-in editor frontend smoke test completed 101 stops.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\n## Compatibility and review questions\nThis is a **draft** because the wire format intentionally replaces the existing Godot 3 remote debugger protocol. The built-in editor is updated, but unmodified external debugger clients will not attach. Maintainer guidance on an opt-in/legacy coexistence strategy is welcome before this is marked ready.\n\nThe companion VS Code client is proposed in [godot-vscode-plugin#1062](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-vscode-plugin/pull/1062). This PR targets `3.6` to match the tested implementation; I can retarget or split it if the project prefers `3.x` or another branch.\n\nRelated Godot 4.6 implementation: #124373.\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null